Project start karne ke steps
1. PostgreSQL service check karo

Windows Start mein Services kholo aur postgresql-x64-16 service Running honi chahiye.


2. Backend start karo — PowerShell 1
cd D:\ProjectReal\CogniHire-main\backend

Get-Content ..\.env | Where-Object { $_ -match '^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=' } | ForEach-Object {
  $key, $value = $_.Split('=', 2)
  [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable($key, $value, 'Process')
}

.\mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run
Started CogniHireApplication dikhne par backend chal raha hai. Is terminal ko khula rehne do.

3. Frontend start karo — PowerShell 2
cd D:\ProjectReal\CogniHire-main\frontend
npm run dev
Agar pehli baar setup hai ya frontend dependencies install nahi hain, pehle npm install chalao.

4. Browser mein kholo

Frontend terminal mein diya URL kholo, usually http://localhost:5173. Pehli baar Create account karke sign in karo.

# $bytes = New-Object byte[] 48
# $rng = [System.Security.Cryptography.RandomNumberGenerator]::Create()
# $rng.GetBytes($bytes)
#[Convert]::ToBase64String($bytes)






#powershell -Command "$b = New-Object byte[] 48; [System.Security.Cryptography.RandomNumberGenerator]::Create().GetBytes($b); [Convert]::ToBase64String($b)"

//PowerShell as Administrator
Start-Service postgresql-x64-16
Test-NetConnection localhost -Port 5432

cd D:\ProjectReal\CogniHire-main
docker compose -f docker-compose.piston.yml up -d

cd D:\ProjectReal\CogniHire-main\backend
.\mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run

cd D:\ProjectReal\CogniHire-main\frontend
npm run dev

cd D:\ProjectReal\CogniHire-main
docker compose -f docker-compose.piston.yml down
docker compose up -d cognihire-redis cognihire-piston
docker compose ps

